<title>USA: Utah 400 MW coal-fired power plant back on line.</title>
<headline>Utah 400 MW coal-fired power plant back on line.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 400-megawatt (MW) coal-fired unit at the Bonanza power plant in Vernal, Utah, is, as expected, back to partial load and should be at full capacity late Wednesday, sources familiar with the plant's operations said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The unit was shut Monday morning for routine repairs, they said.</p>
<p>The Bonanza plant's majority owner is Deseret Generation and Transmission Cooperative.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
</text>
